ases.\n\n### Evidence that would settle it\n* Invoices, supplier agreements, or payroll records corresponding to the $5k\u2013$10k transfers.\n* Corporate registration documents showing legitimate commercial relationships or common ownership among the account holders.\n* Transaction payment memos specifying trade or contract references.\n\n### Weak points in the case\n* **No circular flow:** `money_returns_to_start` is explicitly `false`, contradicting a circular layering or round-tripping scheme.\n* **Inconsistent structuring:** 3 out of 8 transfers fall into the lower $5k\u2013$8k band, undermining the assertion that transfers are intentionally designed to skirt the $10k threshold.\n* **Narrow timeframe:** The activity covers only 7 days (2026-08-13 to 2026-08-20), which is too limited to establish a pattern of illicit intent versus routine operational liquidity settlement for newly opened accounts.", "source": "live", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash"}}}, {"t": 33.66, "ev": {"type": "done", "case_id": "CASE-1018-F8992A", "seconds": 33.3, "queries": 7, "blocked": 1, "audit_entries": 16}}]